    "b60775e6-438f-55a9-9538-753c88735cf8": {
      "type": "StorySegmentLayer",
      "name": "6. 6 Nov 02:30 IST, stagnation sets in",
      "visible": true,
      "parameters": {
        "zoom": 10.46,
        "extent": [
          8506701.53,
          3274212.69,
          8751604.41,
          3382011.46
        ],
        "enableIdentify": true,
        "content": {
          "contentMode": "map",
          "markdown": "<div style='font-size:16px; line-height:1.5; min-height:84vh;'><div style='font-size:.8em; color:#64748b; letter-spacing:.03em; margin:0 0 .5em;'>5 · Night · Weather: Aurora 1.5</div><ul style='margin:0 0 .5em 1.1em; padding:0;'><li style='margin:0 0 .35em 0;'>For the first night Aurora 1.5 puts Anand Vihar's mixing layer as low as <b>137 m</b> with a median wind of <b>11.1 km/h</b>; the short lines on the map are that wind (direction it blows, length its strength).</li><li style='margin:0 0 .35em 0;'>With the same emissions and a thinner layer of air to mix into, surface concentrations rise. That is why nights are worse.</li></ul><div style='background:#0f172a; color:#f8fafc; padding:.5em .8em; border-radius:14px; margin:.5em 0; font-size:.85em; line-height:1.4;'><div style='font-size:.75em; opacity:.7; margin-bottom:.15em;'>📱 Sentence added to the message</div>From night to morning pollution will tend to pool near the surface. Keep windows closed and skip early-morning exercise.</div><div style='background:#e6f3f7; border-left:6px solid #0b6e8f; padding:.45em .7em; border-radius:8px; margin:.5em 0; font-size:.9em; color:#1e293b;'><b style='color:#0b6e8f;'>What this system shows</b> · the hourly stagnation flags are real Aurora 1.5 output from a real initial condition.</div></div>",
          "image": "",
          "imageCaption": "",
          "paneAlignment": "end",
          "panelWidth": "34%"
        },
        "transition": {
          "type": "linear",
          "time": 1.5
