    "11677e63-2e0e-5332-9d7a-2a7ab4b2b711": {
      "type": "StorySegmentLayer",
      "name": "9. What, when, where, why and how in 160 characters",
      "visible": true,
      "parameters": {
        "zoom": 10.46,
        "extent": [
          8506701.53,
          3274212.69,
          8751604.41,
          3382011.46
        ],
        "enableIdentify": true,
        "content": {
          "contentMode": "map",
          "markdown": "<div style='font-size:16px; line-height:1.5; min-height:84vh;'><div style='font-size:.8em; color:#64748b; letter-spacing:.03em; margin:0 0 .5em;'>8 · Message design</div><ul style='margin:0 0 .5em 1.1em; padding:0;'><li style='margin:0 0 .35em 0;'><b>What</b> (value + CPCB category) · <b>when</b> (peak time) · <b>where</b> (site) · <b>how</b> (one or two actions). Short for SMS/push, long for the app and briefings.</li><li style='margin:0 0 .35em 0;'>Category names exactly as CPCB uses them, so they match the news and the official app.</li><li style='margin:0 0 .35em 0;'><b>Name sensitive groups first</b> and add one sentence of weather reasoning; people who understand why nights are worse comply better.</li><li style='margin:0 0 .35em 0;'>GRAP as \"corresponding level\" only; invoking it is CAQM's authority. A fixed disclaimer: \"AI guidance; follow official CPCB/CAQM alerts\".</li></ul><div style='background:#fff4e0; border-left:6px solid #b7791f; padding:.45em .7em; border-radius:8px; margin:.5em 0; font-size:.9em; color:#1e293b;'><b style='color:#b7791f;'>Government and city</b> · the wording is kept where health experts can review and edit it; the issuing authority owns the final text.</div></div>",
          "image": "",
          "imageCaption": "",
          "paneAlignment": "end",
          "panelWidth": "34%"
        },
        "transition": {
          "type": "linear",
          "time": 1.5
        },
