    "60db6f4b-1222-5bd2-bb6a-410cb27994f0": {
      "type": "StorySegmentLayer",
      "name": "11. The truth about resolution, and responsible use",
      "visible": true,
      "parameters": {
        "zoom": 10.46,
        "extent": [
          8506701.53,
          3274212.69,
          8751604.41,
          3382011.46
        ],
        "enableIdentify": true,
        "content": {
          "contentMode": "map",
          "markdown": "<div style='font-size:16px; line-height:1.5; min-height:84vh;'><div style='font-size:.8em; color:#64748b; letter-spacing:.03em; margin:0 0 .5em;'>10 · Limits and responsibility · Pollutants: synthetic example</div><ul style='margin:0 0 .5em 1.1em; padding:0;'><li style='margin:0 0 .35em 0;'>The large square is one cell (0.4°) of the air-pollution model; most of Delhi fits in two or three. <b>Differences between sites are interpolation</b>, not roadside measurements.</li><li style='margin:0 0 .35em 0;'>The hourly concentration curve joins 12-hour forecasts; the hourly structure comes from Aurora 1.5's weather, and the messages say so.</li><li style='margin:0 0 .35em 0;'>In this run the concentrations are a <b>synthetic example</b> (the pollutant data needs an account); the stagnant hours are real model output.</li><li style='margin:0 0 .35em 0;'>Aurora is a research model. It must not drive operational decisions without expert review.</li></ul><div style='background:#fff4e0; border-left:6px solid #b7791f; padding:.45em .7em; border-radius:8px; margin:.5em 0; font-size:.9em; color:#1e293b;'><b style='color:#b7791f;'>Government and city</b> · a real service needs per-station correction or further training on regional data, which presupposes access to the official observations.</div></div>",
          "image": "",
          "imageCaption": "",
          "paneAlignment": "end",
          "panelWidth": "34%"
        },
        "transition": {
          "type": "linear",
          "time": 1.5
